<div class="container py-5">
  <h1 class="mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p class="text-body-secondary small">Last updated: <%= Date.current.to_fs(:long) %></p>

  <p>
    Next Step Assistant (“the app”) stores information you provide so you can manage job applications, projects, and resumes.
    This policy describes what we collect, how it is used, and how you can request deletion.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Data we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information</strong> — Email address and a bcrypt-hashed password. If you use GitHub sign-in, we store your GitHub provider identifier and UID; we may also receive your GitHub email address to create or link your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Job records</strong> — Titles, organizations, deadlines, dates, descriptions, application status, and optional links to uploaded resumes.</li>
    <li><strong>Project records</strong> — Names, descriptions, skills, and GitHub links you enter.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage of app features</strong> — Standard server and session data needed to operate the service (for example, session cookies for signed-in users).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Resume uploads</h2>
  <p>
    Resume files are PDFs you upload voluntarily. They are stored using Rails Active Storage and associated with your account.
    We validate file type and size at upload. Resume PDF content is not sent to external AI services; the in-app Match assistant only uses resume <em>names</em> and filenames for keyword comparison, not the full document text.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">User accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You must sign in to access jobs, projects, and resumes. Data is private to your account; other users cannot view your entries.
    We do not sell your personal information to third parties.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">How we use data</h2>
  <p>
    Data is used solely to provide app functionality: displaying and editing your records, authentication, and the local Match assistant on job pages.
    GitHub OAuth, when enabled, is used only for sign-in through GitHub’s authorization flow.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The production app is hosted on Heroku. Data is stored in the application database and file storage configured for that environment.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Requesting deletion</h2>
  <p>
    To request deletion of your account and associated data (including uploaded resumes), contact the development team by opening an issue on our
    <a href="https://github.com/NU-CS-Software-Studio-Spring-26/project-next-step-assistant/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a>
    or emailing a team member listed in the course project roster. Include the email address tied to your account so we can verify ownership.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will delete or anonymize your account data within a reasonable timeframe after confirming your request. Some backups may persist briefly according to the hosting provider’s retention policies.
  </p>

  <p class="text-body-secondary small mt-4 mb-0">
    <%= link_to "About this app", about_path %> ·
    <a href="https://github.com/NU-CS-Software-Studio-Spring-26/project-next-step-assistant" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
  </p>
</div>
